  "live_records": {
    "q-40560": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40560",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\sqrt{2})(1)+(1)(\\sqrt{2})+(-2)(-5)+(3)(2)}{\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{16}\\sqrt{32}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{32}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
